<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="12a68252">&lt;p&gt;
    Communication has to be two way i.e. by developing feedback mechanisms the practitioner creates the opportunity to hear
    about what is working well, what is not&amp;nbsp;and what needs to be improved going forward. It provides an opportunity to
    the practitioner to address people’s concerns.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    A formal meeting with the project sponsor&amp;nbsp;after the close of the project with the goal to gain feedback on how to
    improve project and program delivery and therefore contribute to, and increase, the value generated by each competency
    area.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Review lessons learned for incorporation with managing project sponsor communication for final report
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Compile documentation to support completion of work and compilation of final report, which documents the executive
        summary, summary of final report, which documents the executive summary, summary of findings, detailed findings and
        the appendix
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Schedule meeting – address logistics such as day, time and location
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Prepare draft final report
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Review draft final report with executive in charge, if appropriate
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Revise draft final report and finalizes same
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Distribute final report to managing project sponsor
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Conduct post implementation review meeting
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
